 ## Follow-ups
 
+- Upstream (devicebasedauth.org `packages/verify`, fix there and re-vendor): `createOidcClient`
+  caches the discovery and JWKS response bodies without checking `response.ok`, so one error
+  response poisons a long-lived client (cronly builds one per link request to avoid it);
+  `createSiteAuth` takes the tightest `spend_usd_per_month` of *every* grant in a credential,
+  including grants for other audiences' namespaces (conservative, but a hashbin cap can cap
+  cronly); `inflate` checks its size bound only after decompressing the whole status list.
+
 - Mark a `dba-key:` row revoked when the verifier reports `revoked`, so queued retries stop
   immediately rather than at credential expiry or unlink.
 - Honor resource-scoped grants (`job:<name>`) per route.
